<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mule xmlns="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core"
	xmlns:http="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http"
	xmlns:ee="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core"
	xmlns:doc="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/documentation"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core/current/mule.xsd
		http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http/current/mule-http.xsd
		http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core/current/mule-ee.xsd">

	<!--
		CONTENT ENRICHER (Hohpe and Woolf): when a message lacks data the receiver needs, the enricher looks the
		data up in another system and adds it to the message. Here an order carries only a customerId; before it
		is invoiced and shipped it needs the customer's name, tier and shipping address, which the customer
		service (CRM, simulated in content-enricher-crm.xml) holds.
		POST /eip/orders/enrich { orderId, customerId, items }
		  -> 200 { orderId, customerId, items, customer: { name, tier, shippingAddress } }

		Mule 3 had an enricher scope; in Mule 4 the enricher is a target variable on the operation. The HTTP
		request below stores the CRM's answer in vars.vCustomer (target), and only its customer part
		(targetValue="#[payload.customer]"; the CRM's metadata is left out). "When you set a variable from an
		operation, the operation outputs to the next component in the flow the same message that it received as
		input", so the order is still the payload after the call, and the Transform merges the two:
		https://docs.mulesoft.com/mule-runtime/latest/target-variables

		When the CRM cannot answer, the order cannot be enriched. The same page states that "target variables are
		not set when an error occurs", so the failed call does not set vars.vCustomer
		(it keeps whatever it held before) and there is no customer to merge. This flow
		then answers 503 { orderId, enrichment: "FAILED", reason } and does not pass the order on without the
		customer: invoicing and shipping need the address. (When the missing data is optional, the other choice
		is to continue with the order marked for a later enrichment.) A customerId the CRM does not know is the
		caller's error: 400.
	-->
	<flow name="order-enrich-with-customer" doc:description="Content enricher: POST /eip/orders/enrich adds the customer's name, tier and shipping address from the CRM to an order that carries only the customerId; 503 when the CRM is unavailable.">
		<http:listener doc:name="POST /eip/orders/enrich" config-ref="http-listener-config" path="/eip/orders/enrich" allowedMethods="POST">
			<http:response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 200]" />
		</http:listener>
		<logger doc:name="INFO: Log enrichment request" level="INFO" message="#['Enrich orderId=' ++ (payload.orderId default 'none') ++ ', correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
		<choice doc:name="Validate Order To Enrich">
			<when expression="#[(not (payload is Object)) or isEmpty(payload.orderId) or isEmpty(payload.customerId) or (not (payload.items is Array)) or isEmpty(payload.items)]">
				<raise-error doc:name="Raise BAD_REQUEST Error - Missing order fields" type="APP:BAD_REQUEST" description="orderId, customerId and a non-empty items array are required" />
			</when>
		</choice>
		<try doc:name="Try Enrich Order With Customer">
			<http:request doc:name="Look Up Customer In CRM" config-ref="eip-self-http-request-config" method="GET" path="/eip/services/customers/{customerId}" target="vCustomer" targetValue="#[payload.customer]">
				<http:uri-params><![CDATA[#[{ customerId: payload.customerId }]]]></http:uri-params>
			</http:request>
			<ee:transform doc:name="Merge Customer Into Order">
				<ee:message>
					<ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
payload ++ {
	customer: {
		name: vars.vCustomer.name,
		tier: vars.vCustomer.tier,
		shippingAddress: vars.vCustomer.shippingAddress
	}
}]]></ee:set-payload>
				</ee:message>
			</ee:transform>
			<error-handler>
				<on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (customer not found)" type="HTTP:NOT_FOUND" logException="false">
					<set-variable doc:name="SET httpStatus" variableName="httpStatus" value="400" />
					<ee:transform doc:name="Build Unknown Customer Error">
						<ee:message>
							<ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{ error: "customer " ++ payload.customerId ++ " not found" }]]></ee:set-payload>
						</ee:message>
					</ee:transform>
				</on-error-continue>
				<on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (CRM unavailable)" type="HTTP:SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE, HTTP:CONNECTIVITY, HTTP:TIMEOUT" logException="false">
					<logger doc:name="WARN: Log enrichment failed" level="WARN" message="#['Order ' ++ payload.orderId ++ ' not enriched: ' ++ error.errorType.namespace ++ ':' ++ error.errorType.identifier ++ ', correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
					<set-variable doc:name="SET httpStatus" variableName="httpStatus" value="503" />
					<ee:transform doc:name="Build Enrichment Failed Response">
						<ee:message>
							<ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
	orderId: payload.orderId,
	enrichment: "FAILED",
	// The error type only: the description names the requester's URL.
	reason: error.errorType.namespace ++ ":" ++ error.errorType.identifier
}]]></ee:set-payload>
						</ee:message>
					</ee:transform>
				</on-error-continue>
			</error-handler>
		</try>
	</flow>
</mule>
